WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.839
So now that we've talked about shutdowns,
let's talk about why we have them and why

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:10.050
we are not in a position to open in any significant
way.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:12.180
We're not doing enough testing.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:16.430
Some of the tests don't have a quick enough
turnaround time and we don't have a proper

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.540
contact tracing infrastructure.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.280
And I know that this may be boring stuff,
but I think it's important to go through so

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.910
that it's not a mystery to anybody.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:31.160
We are not unable to open because governors
are authoritarian dictators, that that's not

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.450
why when we see other countries starting to
open up.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:39.469
And yet here we have so many health experts
say we're just not anywhere close to ready.

00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:43.999
The reason is that the Trump administration
hasn't built a proper testing system or a

00:00:43.999 --> 00:00:49.909
proper contact tracing system, despite constantly
bragging that we have the best tests and the

00:00:49.909 --> 00:00:51.590
most tests and all of this stuff.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:52.700
So let's explore it.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.530
Why do we need more tests to open?

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.250
We have about a million official cases right
now, a little more than that closing in on

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.870
1.1 million.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:06.140
Every antibody tests that's been done so far
suggests that the real rate of cases is at

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:11.320
least three times the official rate, maybe
as many as 20 or 30 times the official rate.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:15.560
So what that means is we're only testing a
fraction of the people who have the virus.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.189
This means you have likely millions of people
who don't know that they have it, who are

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:23.869
going around spreading it, especially the
asymptomatic people.

00:01:23.869 --> 00:01:28.259
If we were testing at really high levels,
you could ensure that everyone who has any

00:01:28.259 --> 00:01:31.649
symptoms at minimum could get tested and know
if they have it.

00:01:31.649 --> 00:01:35.939
If the turnaround of the tests was uniformly
faster, people could learn more quickly that

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:40.189
they have it and immediately quarantine as
opposed to maybe quarantining, maybe saying

00:01:40.189 --> 00:01:42.429
add or know that I have it, I'm gonna keep
walking around.

00:01:42.429 --> 00:01:49.130
And if you had proper contact tracing infrastructure,
you could immediately contact the individuals

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:54.990
that had been potentially exposed by every
new case and say, hey, your friend, your coworker

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.780
or whatever has been exposed has tested positive.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.049
You now need to isolate for 14 days.

00:02:00.049 --> 00:02:01.310
This is what South Korea did.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:04.069
And they had their first case on the same
day that we did.

00:02:04.069 --> 00:02:06.690
Now, what is the truth about testing levels?

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.550
Because there's a lot of disinformation here.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:15.110
Dr. Foushee has said we need to be testing
at roughly 3 to 4 million tests per week to

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.900
realistically think about opening.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:22.660
So in the last seven days, we have tested
1.5 million people.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:27.090
That's an average of two hundred and twenty
two thousand people per day.

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:29.280
This is better than early April, no doubt.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.800
In the first seven days of April, we averaged
one hundred and forty three thousand tests.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:37.890
Today, in the last week, we've averaged two
hundred and twenty two thousand, an improvement

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.430
of about 50 percent.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.440
But it's been an entire month.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.600
They said by the end of March we would have
tested tens of millions of people.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:49.880
That date came and went and we are still only
testing about two hundred and twenty thousand

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:50.880
a day.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:57.030
So as a bare minimum, as an absolute bare
minimum, we have to test 500000 thousand people

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:02.460
per day reliably, which is more than twice
where we are right now.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:06.540
There are public health experts who say we
really need a million tests today.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.700
There is one model that says we need 20 million
tests per day.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:15.580
I mean, that's science fiction at this point,
particularly until you have an antigen test.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:19.270
Right now we have RNA tests, until you have
antigen tests.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:23.260
It would be very difficult, really impossible
to test at that level.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:29.070
So instead of actually increasing testing,
Donald Trump spends his time bragging and

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.070
lying.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:35.870
Even this morning, Donald Trump tweeted, quote,
We are doing far more and better testing than

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:38.200
any other country in the world.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:43.010
And yet the media does nothing but complain,
no matter how good a job is done.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:44.750
The same as with the ventilators.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:48.010
They will never say we are doing a great job.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:51.900
They will only viciously gripe the data's
public.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:58.780
If you look at the top testing per capita,
the United States is forty third in the world

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.510
in testing per capita.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:03.740
We're behind Belgium, but we're ahead of Belarus.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:07.680
Now, some people say you can't really compare
the US to the Faroe Islands.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.750
You have to eliminate the tiny countries from
that list.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:16.930
Well, OK, if you concede that the US as a
country is twenty seventh in the world among

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:19.070
reasonably sized countries.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:22.100
So we are nowhere near the top of the numbers
are public.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:30.600
If you're out there complaining about my state
isn't open, my governor is a dictator or whatever.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.820
Just look at testing.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:37.470
If Trump spent half the time that he spends
bragging about testing actually working to

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:41.500
increase tests, we could be testing five hundred
thousand a day by now.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:47.470
We could be testing 750000 a day by now, and
we could be having more reasonable conversations

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.430
about actually opening up.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:54.620
This is why we are not ready to open in any
significant way at this point in time.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:55.620
Let me know your thoughts.

